# A shop with a cart: records, a function, a screen shown inside another with an input, a list of rows,
# When / Otherwise, boxes, a press that stops with a message, and a number box given text that is not a number.
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "Name" "Pear"
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "Price" "2"
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "Name" "Fig"
# do: type "Price" "x"
# do: type "Price" "3.5"
# do: type "Price" "3"
# do: press "Add"
# do: type "Coupon code" "SAVE"
# do: press "Clear"
# do: press "Back"

An Item has:
  Name is text
  Price is number

To add up:
  Receive items as a list of Item
  Set sum to 0
  For each item in items:
    Increase sum by item's price
  Give sum

Screen Shop:
  Remember cart as a list of Item, starting at []
  Remember name as text, starting at ""
  Remember price starting at 0
  Show a heading "Shop"
  Show a text box "Name" for name
  Show a number box "Price" for price
  Show a button "Add" (off when name is empty):
    When pressed:
      When price is at most 0:
        Stop with "The price must be more than 0"
      Add an Item with name name and price price to cart
      Set name to ""
  Show Cart:
    items: cart

Screen Cart:
  Receive items as a list of Item, title as text ("Your cart" if not given)
  Remember coupon as text, starting at ""
  Show a heading: title
  When items is empty:
    Show "Your cart is empty"
  Otherwise:
    Show a list with each item in items:
      Show a row:
        Show item's name
        Show item's price
    Show "Total: {add up with items}"
  Show a text box "Coupon code" for coupon
  Show a button "Clear" (off when coupon is empty):
    When pressed:
      Set coupon to ""
  Show a button "Back" that opens Shop
